From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Pipeline cache: a run-time pipeline build tells the front's heap, so its requests can wait for memory (EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_GPU_MS)

A crash in free play on 10 Nov 2026 22:07 (leaving Kokiri Forest, pool empty): 64 pipelines were built on
the GPU thread in the last 4 s. EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_MS only covers the "VkPipeline..." threads; the
GPU thread's requests came back empty at once, and a pipeline that cannot be built is left out with
its draws.

The two run-time entry points (CreateGraphicsPipeline() and the compute one that reports its build)
now mark their span with eden_heap_wait_scope, a weak call into the PS5 front. With
EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_GPU_MS=<n> the front lets a request inside that span wait up to n ms, once per
build. Without the front or the switch nothing changes.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 93aba85..448f729 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -2941,7 +2941,31 @@ void PipelineCache::WarnKeptPointer(size_t program, u64 slot) const {
     }
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_GPU_MS (the PS5 front's heap, headless/heap_arenas.inc): while a thread builds a
+// pipeline itself at run time, a request of its the heap cannot serve waits for memory instead of
+// coming back empty, as the builder threads' requests do under EDEN_UP_HEAP_WAIT_MS. The front
+// has to know when that is: these two calls say so. Without the front, or without the switch,
+// nothing changes.
+extern "C" void eden_heap_wait_scope(int enter) __attribute__((weak));
+namespace {
+struct HeapWaitScope {
+    HeapWaitScope() {
+        if (eden_heap_wait_scope) {
+            eden_heap_wait_scope(1);
+        }
+    }
+    ~HeapWaitScope() {
+        if (eden_heap_wait_scope) {
+            eden_heap_wait_scope(0);
+        }
+    }
+    HeapWaitScope(const HeapWaitScope&) = delete;
+    HeapWaitScope& operator=(const HeapWaitScope&) = delete;
+};
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
+    const HeapWaitScope heap_wait;
     Common::HangSite site{"building a graphics pipeline"};
     const auto begin = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     const u64 key_hash = graphics_key.Hash();
@@ -3505,6 +3529,7 @@ void PipelineCache::SerializeTranslatedGraphicsPipeline(std::list<TranslationJob
 std::unique_ptr<ComputePipeline> PipelineCache::CreateComputePipeline(
     const ComputePipelineCacheKey& key, const ShaderInfo* shader,
     const ComputePipeline* previous) {
+    const HeapWaitScope heap_wait;
     Common::HangSite site{"building a compute pipeline"};
     const auto begin = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     SCOPE_EXIT {
